---
import SimplePage from '../../components/SimplePage.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
---

<SimplePage lang="en" route="privacy" title="Privacy policy">
  <p>
    This privacy policy explains which personal data is processed when you visit this website and when you send an
    inquiry through the contact form, for what purpose, and which rights you have.
  </p>

  <h2>Controller</h2>
  <p>
    Forma Studio<br />
    Switzerland<br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
  </p>
  <p>For any question about data protection, an email to this address is sufficient.</p>

  <h2>Which data is processed</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Details you provide yourself through the contact form or by email</li>
    <li>Technical connection data that arises at the hosting provider when the website is accessed</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Contact form</h2>
  <p>When the contact form is submitted, the following details are transmitted:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Name</li>
    <li>Email address</li>
    <li>Business (optional)</li>
    <li>Service required (optional)</li>
    <li>Budget range (optional)</li>
    <li>Project description</li>
    <li>Confirmation of consent and the language version of the website used</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The details are transmitted through the form service of the hosting provider Netlify and stored there. If email
    notifications are set up, submissions may additionally be forwarded to Forma Studio by email. Submissions are
    checked automatically to protect against spam; Netlify uses the spam-filtering service Akismet for this.
  </p>

  <h2>Purpose of processing</h2>
  <p>
    The details from the contact form are used to process and answer your inquiry and, if a collaboration results from
    it, to prepare and carry out the project. They are not used for advertising and are not sold.
  </p>

  <h2>Retention</h2>
  <p>
    Contact inquiries are retained only for as long as necessary to process the inquiry. If a business relationship
    results from the inquiry, the data is retained for as long as necessary for that relationship and the applicable
    legal retention obligations.
  </p>

  <h2>Hosting with Netlify</h2>
  <p>
    This website is hosted by Netlify, Inc. (USA). When the website is accessed, Netlify as the hosting provider
    processes technically necessary connection data. This may include in particular the IP address, the date and time of
    access, the page requested, and details of the browser and operating system. This data is required to operate and
    secure the website.
  </p>

  <h2>Recipients and service providers</h2>
  <p>Personal data is passed only to the following service providers, as far as needed to operate the website:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Netlify, Inc. (USA): hosting of the website and processing of form submissions</li>
    <li>
      Google (Gmail): the Forma Studio email inbox for inquiries sent by email and, if set up, for notifications about
      form submissions
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Data transfers abroad</h2>
  <p>
    Netlify and Google are US providers and operate servers in various countries. Personal data may therefore also be
    processed outside Switzerland, in particular in the USA.
  </p>

  <h2>Cookies, analytics and tracking</h2>
  <p>
    This website currently sets no cookies and uses no analytics or tracking services. Fonts and images are loaded
    directly from this website and not from external providers.
  </p>

  <h2>External links</h2>
  <p>
    The website contains links to the demo websites of the concept projects. These open as separate websites in a new
    tab.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Within the scope of applicable data protection law, you can in particular request information about the data
    processed about you, have incorrect data corrected, request the deletion of your data, and withdraw consent you have
    given. An email to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> is sufficient.
  </p>
  <p>
    You may also contact the competent data protection supervisory authority. In Switzerland, this is the Federal Data
    Protection and Information Commissioner (FDPIC).
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    This privacy policy may be updated if the website or the services used change. The version published here applies.
  </p>

  <h2>Last updated</h2>
  <p>October 2026</p>
</SimplePage>
